{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/772153-home-brew-demonic-defenses-against-those-of-twilight","id":772153,"title":"[Home-brew] Demonic defenses against those of twilight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T00:57:35-08:00","id":772153,"title":"[Home-brew] Demonic defenses against those of twilight","content":"Demons I feel are quite under prepared for anything in twilight. Yes I understand that it adds to part of the worry and paranoia surrounding angels but the scary part about angels is not just that they can be watching you from twilight but that just like a demon an angel could be in cover, an angel could be anyone. So I have come up with three powers, 2 embeds and 1 exploit that could potentially assist a demon in dealing with entities in twilight. These home-brewed embeds and exploit are still rough and are more the initial concepts so any feedback is welcome.<br /> <hr /><br /> <u>Lift the veil</u> (embed, instrumental )<br /> Some angels while in physical form are required to still be able to cast their senses into twilight for reasons related to their mission and demons who remember the pathways of this embed can have access to this same capacity. Unlike the version used by angels in physical form though this version has notable flaws. Maybe the machine filled in the gaps before but a demon casting their senses into twilight receives a penalty to perceiving anything not in twilight. The other flaw it has is either because the machine saw no need to perceive its own agents or intentionally omitted the capacity so though a demon with this embed can perceive a ghost or spirit an angel still hides from sight.<br /> <br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Intelligence + Occult<br /> <br /> Notes<br /> - Unsure if it should have to tune to specific frequencies or if a general use is better.<br /> - Unsure if the restriction on perceiving angels is completely warranted or if the ability would be fine without the restriction.<br /> <hr /><br /> <u>Shadow whispers</u> ( embed, vocal )<br /> Mortals through long standing traditions and ritual can assist a ghost or spirit in appearing before them. There is an underlying system at work here. A system that demons are capable of tapping into and exploiting. A demon who uses this embed is avoiding the rituals required and deliberately triggering the progression of conditions to allow a ghost or spirit to manifest before the demon. Each use of this embed will progress the revenant condition by a stage towards manifestation ( nothing -&gt; anchor / resonant -&gt; open -&gt; willing manifestation) but at the cost of potentially drawing attention. Each use in a day whether successful or not will result in a risk of compromise starting at +1 with a penalty of an additional -1 with each use ( First: +1, Second: 0, Third: -1 etc)<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Presence + Occult<br /> <br /> Notes<br /> - Restriction on angels again but more because of the madness of such an attempt<br /> <hr /><br /> Call to form ( exploit, Prerequisite: Shadow whispers)<br /> Demons have so little to combat an immaterial being so why not make that which is immaterial, solid? This exploit builds on exploiting the framework that mortals relief on to bring the ephemeral before them but skips to the final step. The more a demon knows about the being in question the easier the task of forcing the being to manifest and be locked temporally in such a state. If a demon succeeds in this attempt the being is locked in a manifested state for an hour per success more the demon has over the target.<br /> <br /> Cost: 3 aether<br /> Roll: 1/turn<br /> Action: Extended<br /> <br /> Presence + Occult + Primum ( + / - based on knowledge) vs Resistance + Rank<br /> <br /> Possible bonuses to the roll if the demon knows the entities ban(s), bane(s)<br /> Possible pentalies to the roll if the demon does not know the entries type (angel, ghost etc), name<br /> <br /> Notes<br /> - Still debating if it is better as a contested power or with a flat penalty based on the entries rank","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}